just like with a superhero batman we've  seen quite a few versions of catwoman  also known as selena kyle over the years  from julie newmar and arthur kit in the  batman tv series starring adam west and  burt ward to michelle pfeiffer and anne  hathaway in more modern film adaptations  there have been many changes to the  character over time so when it was  announced as zoe kravitz would be taking  on the iconic character for the new the  batman movie fans should have known to  expect something new in the batman fans  get to see a younger bruce wayne played  by robert pattinson in his early years  as a vigilante and that's the same case  with selena she isn't quite catwoman yet  though she's well on her way while she  has all of the skills and the drive to  become the well-known anti-hero she's  still just a young woman with some  personal issues to take care of but what  else does a 2022 film change about  selena while there are a few stark  changes for the character to know with  kravitz's performance there's one  glaring difference that drives the whole  movie forward beware spoilers ahead in  the original dc catwoman comics selena's  parents are maria and brian kyle who  both tragically die when she is quite  young leading to her life on the street  but the version of selena we see in the  batman doesn't quite have the same  experience yes her mother is maria but  her father is someone very different  it's noted by many that the comics  include speculation that selena's real  parents aren't the kyles but are really  carmine falcone and his wife louisa  while the comics never explicitly  confirm or deny this the batman decides  to concretely change the story and have  falcone be selena's father in the movie  maria works at the iceberg lounge and  has a relationship of sorts with a mob  boss which results in selena's birth  there is zero mention of her comic book  father brian and it seems unlikely that  there ever would be impossible future  films selena is completely sure that  falcone is her father but after being  abandoned by him after her mother's  death which she later finds out as his  doing she has no real attachment to the  man though she holds strong feelings of  resentment and anger so when bruce  uncovers the true death of falcone's  crimes selena is ever so eager to find  falcone and take him down stopping him  from doing anything else while also  getting a chance to confront him about  her mother add to that they reveal that  he's involved in her roommate's death  and you've got just about the worst  father-daughter relationship out there  but aside from the connection with  falcone the batman also makes one other  small yet important change to selena  while this is a very small detail in the  movie longtime fans of catwoman in the  dc comics might notice something about  the way selena interacts with her  roommate and co-worker from the iceberg  lounge the detail is actually a change  from past screen depictions of selena  but it makes the character more similar  to the comic book version luckily for  those who missed it matt galea of  pedestrian did not picking up on hints  of an intimate relationship between the  two women especially in how selena calls  her baby selena is frequently depicted  as bisexual in the comics which has made  canon in catwoman issue 39 so while the  batman definitely doesn't confirm  selena's sexuality there are hints that  this aspect of the character may be  explored in further films galia was able  to ask both kravitz and director matt  reeves about this specific detail  directly and whether or not it was a  purposeful choice in order to highlight  her bisexuality in the comics kravitz  confirmed to galea for pedestrian that  although it wasn't in the script that's  definitely the way i interpreted that  that they had some kind of romantic  relationship reeves wasn't as definitive  with his comments but he did say that i  don't think we meant to go directly in  that way but you can interpret it that  way for sure there was meant to be quite  an intimate relationship between them  based on this it's certainly worth  hoping that if reeves kravitz and others  return for future installments after the  batman selena's sexuality will finally  be accurately presented on screen check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  batman are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one
 

